From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan E <76752281+ThaRae@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 16:46:41 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] LibWebView+WebContent: Add a fingerprinting protection
 setting

The setting is on by default and lives next to Global Privacy Control:
about:settings has a toggle for it, pages are told through their view
as they are about GPC, and workers are told by the worker agent manager
when they start and whenever it changes, as they are about the
languages. In test mode it is always reported as off.

The same message carries the secret farbling is keyed with. The browser
makes it once per run, so every WebContent process gives a site the
same values.
